    "narrative": "Today\u2019s roster construction for the Austin Waves is anchored by the favorable matchups facing **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**, who provide the highest efficiency scores of the day at 85.90 and 74.43, respectively. Both benefit significantly from a plus-matchup against Sugano (xERA 4.93), with park factors and opponent skill metrics providing a combined +33% boost to their base projections. **Drake Baldwin** also emerges as a high-upside play (71.20); despite a standard matchup against Ober, his spot at the top of the order (+10%) and an excellent xwOBA of 0.373 make him a high-efficiency engine for Runs production today.\n\nThe middle of our infield presents a tactical challenge against left-handed starters. While **Coby Mayo** (52.72) maintains a respectable score due to positive platoon adjustments, **Gunnar Henderson** (50.62) and **Sam Antonacci** (42.58) face heavy headwinds against McClanahan and Imanaga. **Gunnar Henderson** is suppressed by a -15% dynamic platoon hit, yet he remains in the lineup due to his high talent floor. **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.60) is the most interesting case; despite a marginal score, his elite sprint speed keeps him in the optimal lineup to secure scarce Stolen Bases, even though his matchup against Buehler suppresses his power output. **Liam Hicks** and **Miguel Vargas** remain in the lineup with scores hovering near 51, providing necessary positional stability, though they offer minimal ceiling given the specific SP constraints.\n\nThe decision to bench our depth pieces was straightforward, as **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remain sidelined on the IL, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara** were held out due to rest or lack of viable matchup opportunities. **Sam Antonacci** barely clung to his roster spot; had his platoon disadvantage against Imanaga been marginally deeper, we would have looked to pivot. No major weather concerns are currently impacting play, but with the high number of left-handed starters opposing us today, we must monitor the bullpen usage late in these games to ensure our primary hitters are not exposed to high-leverage late-inning relievers.",
